          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "India's Draft IT Rules Draw Criticism for Expanding Content Blocking Powers With No Transparency Safeguards",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "The Hindu's editorial analysis of India's draft amendments to the Information Technology Rules warns that proposed changes represent a significant tightening of state control over the digital public sphere, departing from existing judicial rulings on free expression. The draft rules would expand the government's ability to block online content — including AI-generated material — without adequate transparency requirements, due process, or independent review mechanisms. Legal experts cited in the piece argue that the amendments risk enabling digital overreach at a scale that could chill legitimate speech for millions of internet users in India.",
            "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/op-ed/a-tightening-of-the-fist-in-indias-digital-public-square/article70913381.ece",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
